  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For consistency with the groupId now used for the Fedora Repository project, change all packages starting with \"fedora.\" to \"org.fcrepo.\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is not only a Java change.  It will also require changes to poms, assemblies, and possibly other xml files in the codebase.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "[ Impact ]",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) People using fedora.client.FedoraClient in their code will need to use the newly-named class.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Legacy LLStore plugins will need to be updated.  Preferably to plug in via Akubra, but if that can't be done, we should try to provide a solution that allows the use of these older plugins (like a legacy llstore jar, and an akubra adapter)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) Other alternative classes/modules for Fedora will need to be compiled with the new interface/class names.  For example, if people have developed their own DDLGenerator implementations that are maintained outside the main codebase, those will need to be slightly changed and re-compiled to make them work.  The release notes should have a general note about this.  However, cases like #2 may come up in the process of doing this, where we decide a \"legacy adapter\" approach would be helpful, so people don't have to change thier code.  None are currently known.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
